Bootstrap: docker
From: rocker/rstudio:4.4.0

# =============================================================================
# MapMetSC — Apptainer image for the R-based single-cell analysis (Lazic et al.)
# =============================================================================
#
# This definition builds the full R environment "from scratch" on top of the
# same pinned base the project's Dockerfile uses (rocker/rstudio:4.4.0), rather
# than wrapping the pre-built `lazdaria/mapmetsc:v1.0` image on Docker Hub. That
# choice is what lets a SINGLE image run everything:
#
#   * analysis/            (01_read_data ... 06.*_correlation)
#   * analysis_AD/         (01_read_data ... 04_phenotyping)
#   * analysis/07_spatial_analysis.Rmd
#
# Why one image is enough (the testInteractions story)
# ----------------------------------------------------
# The project historically shipped a SECOND image (`lazdaria/mapmetsc_spatial`)
# only because of a bug in imcRtools::testInteractions in versions < 1.5.5. That
# fix first appears in the released imcRtools 1.6.0 (Bioconductor 3.17). This
# image pins Bioconductor to 3.19 (the release matching the base image's frozen
# CRAN snapshot), which provides imcRtools 1.10.0 — well past the fix. The only
# imcRtools function the
# non-spatial scripts use is read_steinbock(), whose API is unchanged across
# these versions, so upgrading to the fixed imcRtools does not affect the rest
# of the pipeline. The %post section asserts imcRtools >= 1.6.0 so a build can
# never silently produce the buggy version.
#
# Build:   apptainer build mapmetsc.sif mapmetsc.def
# Run:     apptainer exec --bind <singlecelldata>:/mnt/data mapmetsc.sif \
#              Rscript run_analysis.R
# (see apptainer/README.md and %help for RStudio + spatial-analysis usage)
# =============================================================================

%labels
    Maintainer      TaschnerMandl / Lazic Group (Apptainer port)
    Description     MapMetSC single-cell + spatial analysis (Lazic et al.)
    Base            rocker/rstudio:4.4.0 (R 4.4.0, Bioconductor 3.19)
    imcRtools       >= 1.6.0 (testInteractions fix; base provides 1.10.0)

%post
    set -e
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # System libraries. Superset of the project Dockerfile plus the extra
    # dev headers needed by packages that image never installed:
    #   EBImage        -> libtiff, libjpeg, libpng, libfftw3
    #   ggrastr/ragg   -> libpng, libfreetype6, libharfbuzz, libfribidi, fontconfig
    #   tiff            -> libtiff
    #   sf/terra (spatial deps) -> libgdal, libproj, libudunits2
    #   igraph          -> libglpk
    #   magick (cytomapper) -> libmagick++
    # Runtime shared libs that Posit *binary* packages dlopen at load time
    # (missing these builds fine but fails at runtime, e.g. library(git2r)):
    #   git2r (needed by workflowr, loaded from .Rprofile) -> libgit2
    #   sf (imcRtools / lisaClust)                          -> libgeos
    #   V8 (transitive dependency)                          -> libnode
    # Plus the rendering toolchain the pipeline needs from a bare Rscript:
    #   rmarkdown::render -> pandoc (rocker bundles it with RStudio Server, but
    #                        it is NOT on PATH outside an RStudio session)
    #   figures use dev="png" -> the cairo device needs system fonts
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    apt-get -y update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        apt-utils \
        ca-certificates curl git \
        pandoc \
        fonts-dejavu-core fonts-liberation \
        libarchive-dev \
        libcairo2-dev \
        libcurl4-openssl-dev \
        libfftw3-dev \
        libfontconfig1-dev \
        libfreetype6-dev \
        libfribidi-dev \
        libgdal-dev \
        libgeos-dev \
        libgit2-dev \
        libglpk-dev \
        libgsl-dev \
        libharfbuzz-dev \
        libjpeg-dev \
        libmagick++-dev \
        libnode-dev \
        libpng-dev \
        libproj-dev \
        libssl-dev \
        libtiff-dev \
        libudunits2-dev \
        libxml2-dev \
        libxt-dev \
        libzstd-dev \
        zlib1g-dev
    apt-get clean
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # R packages. CRAN installs come from the rocker base's pinned Posit
    # Package Manager snapshot (2024-06-13; reproducible, mostly binary).
    #
    # Bioconductor is PINNED to 3.19 to match that CRAN snapshot. BiocManager
    # would otherwise default to 3.20, whose packages need CRAN packages newer
    # than the frozen snapshot (e.g. matrixStats >= 1.4.1) and fail to resolve.
    # Bioc 3.19 also provides imcRtools 1.10.0 (which has the testInteractions
    # fix). The Bioconductor 3.19 repos are added to options(repos) directly and
    # installed with plain install.packages() - this deliberately avoids
    # BiocManager's version-switch handshake, which on a proxied HPC fails twice
    # over: it must download BiocVersion from bioconductor.org (which 504s), and
    # it wants to "downgrade" packages - and it blocks before downloading
    # anything. install.packages() has no such handshake, so only the
    # intermittent 504s on real tarballs remain, which the retry-only-missing
    # loop absorbs. A final completeness check aborts the build if anything is
    # still missing.
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    Rscript - <<'RSCRIPT'
options(
    Ncpus   = min(parallel::detectCores(), 8L),  # parallel, capped to avoid OOM
    timeout = 600                                 # big tarballs on slow mirrors
)
Sys.setenv(R_BIOC_VERSION = "3.19")   # also pins BiocManager for interactive use

installed_ok <- function(pkgs)
    vapply(pkgs, requireNamespace, logical(1), quietly = TRUE)

# Retry an installer, each round attempting only the packages that are still
# missing (optionally sleeping between rounds), so intermittent download
# failures - e.g. 504s from bioconductor.org behind an HPC egress proxy -
# self-heal instead of aborting the whole build.
retry_install <- function(pkgs, installer, tries = 12L, label = "install", sleep = 0) {
    for (i in seq_len(tries)) {
        todo <- pkgs[!installed_ok(pkgs)]
        if (!length(todo)) return(invisible(TRUE))
        if (i > 1L && sleep > 0) Sys.sleep(sleep)
        message(sprintf("[%s] attempt %d/%d - %d remaining: %s",
                        label, i, tries, length(todo),
                        paste(todo, collapse = ", ")))
        try(installer(todo), silent = FALSE)
    }
    invisible(!length(pkgs[!installed_ok(pkgs)]))
}

## --- helpers first --------------------------------------------------------
retry_install(c("remotes", "BiocManager"), install.packages, tries = 4L,
              label = "bootstrap")

## Add the Bioconductor 3.19 repositories next to the rocker CRAN snapshot so a
## plain install.packages() resolves the whole tree. This deliberately does NOT
## call BiocManager::install(version=): that handshake must fetch BiocVersion
## from bioconductor.org (which 504s here) and "downgrade" packages, so it
## blocks before downloading anything. install.packages() has no such handshake.
options(repos = c(
    getOption("repos"),                                  # CRAN = rocker snapshot
    BioCsoft      = "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.19/bioc",
    BioCann       = "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.19/data/annotation",
    BioCexp       = "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.19/data/experiment",
    BioCworkflows = "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.19/workflows"
))

## Bioconductor first: some CRAN packages (e.g. tidyHeatmap) depend on Bioc
## packages, so install those before the CRAN-only batch. Many retries plus a
## short sleep ride out bioconductor.org's intermittent 504s.
bioc_pkgs <- c(
    "SingleCellExperiment", "SpatialExperiment", "SummarizedExperiment",
    "imcRtools", "cytomapper", "CATALYST", "scater", "scuttle",
    "dittoSeq", "batchelor", "lisaClust", "diffcyt", "SingleR",
    "ComplexHeatmap", "BiocParallel", "BioQC", "edgeR", "EBImage",
    "tidyHeatmap"                     # CRAN pkg, but needs ComplexHeatmap (Bioc)
)
retry_install(bioc_pkgs, install.packages, tries = 25L, label = "bioc", sleep = 8)

## --- CRAN -----------------------------------------------------------------
cran_pkgs <- c(
    # rendering / project
    "rmarkdown", "knitr", "workflowr",
    # io
    "readxl", "writexl", "openxlsx",
    # tidyverse + plotting
    "tidyverse", "patchwork", "cowplot", "ggrepel", "ggridges",
    "ggrastr", "ggdendro", "ggpubr", "scales", "viridis",
    "RColorBrewer", "paletteer", "circlize", "colorspace",
    "pheatmap", "gridExtra", "gridGraphics", "hexbin",
    # stats / clustering / models
    "mclust", "harmony", "lme4", "gtools", "rstatix",
    "factoextra", "FactoMineR", "bruceR",
    # single cell (CRAN side)
    "Seurat", "SeuratObject", "uwot", "tiff", "Matrix"
)
retry_install(cran_pkgs, install.packages, tries = 6L, label = "cran")

## --- GitHub (pinned commit, as in the original Dockerfile) ---------------
retry_install("Rphenoannoy", function(pkgs)
    remotes::install_github(
        "stuchly/Rphenoannoy@8b81e2e7fb0599f45070e2cba1b28ac219b7c472",
        upgrade = "never"),
    tries = 4L, label = "github")

## --- Completeness + version assertions -----------------------------------
required <- unique(c(cran_pkgs, bioc_pkgs, "Rphenoannoy"))
missing  <- required[!installed_ok(required)]
if (length(missing)) {
    message("MISSING PACKAGES: ", paste(missing, collapse = ", "))
    quit(status = 1L)
}

## requireNamespace() only loads a namespace; it does NOT dlopen a package's
## compiled shared object. Posit binary packages link against system libraries
## (git2r->libgit2, sf->libgeos, V8->libnode), so a missing runtime lib installs
## fine yet fails on load. Actually ATTACH the startup + shared-lib packages here
## so any such gap fails the BUILD instead of at `.Rprofile`/render time.
for (p in c("git2r", "workflowr", "sf", "imcRtools")) {
    ok <- tryCatch({ suppressPackageStartupMessages(library(p, character.only = TRUE)); TRUE },
                   error = function(e) { message("LOAD ERROR for ", p, ": ", conditionMessage(e)); FALSE })
    if (!ok) quit(status = 1L)
}

## The pipeline renders every step with rmarkdown::render, which needs pandoc
## (rocker bundles it with RStudio Server but not on PATH for a bare Rscript)
## and a cairo-usable font for dev="png". Smoke-test the whole chain at build.
{
    td  <- tempfile(fileext = ".Rmd")
    writeLines(c("---", "title: smoke", "output: html_document", "---", "",
                 "```{r, dev='png'}", "plot(1:3, main = 'ok'); 1 + 1", "```"), td)
    ok <- tryCatch({ rmarkdown::render(td, quiet = TRUE, output_dir = tempdir()); TRUE },
                   error = function(e) { message("RENDER ERROR (pandoc/fonts?): ",
                                                  conditionMessage(e)); FALSE })
    if (!ok) quit(status = 1L)
    cat("rmarkdown render OK (pandoc + png device found).\n")
}

## The whole point of a single image: the fixed testInteractions.
imc_v <- as.character(utils::packageVersion("imcRtools"))
cat("Bioconductor:", Sys.getenv("R_BIOC_VERSION"),
    "| imcRtools:", imc_v, "\n")
if (utils::packageVersion("imcRtools") < "1.6.0") {
    message("imcRtools ", imc_v, " is older than 1.6.0 and still has the ",
            "testInteractions bug; refusing to build.")
    quit(status = 1L)
}
if (!"testInteractions" %in% getNamespaceExports("imcRtools")) {
    message("imcRtools::testInteractions not found; refusing to build.")
    quit(status = 1L)
}
cat("All", length(required), "packages installed; imcRtools OK.\n")
RSCRIPT

    # Leave a lightweight manifest in the image for provenance.
    # (statements separated by real newlines - backslash-continuations inside a
    #  single-quoted -e string are passed verbatim to R and are a syntax error.)
    Rscript -e 'writeLines(capture.output(sessionInfo()), "/opt/mapmetsc-sessionInfo.txt")
ip <- as.data.frame(installed.packages()[, c("Package", "Version")])
write.csv(ip, "/opt/mapmetsc-packages.csv", row.names = FALSE)'

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export LANG=C.UTF-8
    # Headless rendering: no X server inside the container.
    export R_ENABLE_JIT=0
    # Keep interactive BiocManager use pinned to the release the image was built
    # against (matches the frozen CRAN snapshot; imcRtools 1.10.0).
    export R_BIOC_VERSION=3.19

%runscript
    # `apptainer run img.sif`            -> interactive R
    # `apptainer run img.sif Rscript x`  -> runs the given command
    if [ $# -eq 0 ]; then
        exec R --no-save
    else
        exec "$@"
    fi

%test
    # Sanity check executed at the end of `apptainer build`.
    Rscript -e '
        pkgs <- c("imcRtools","cytomapper","CATALYST","lisaClust","diffcyt",
                  "SingleR","ComplexHeatmap","Seurat","harmony","batchelor",
                  "EBImage","ggdendro","ggrastr","tidyverse","Rphenoannoy")
        ok <- vapply(pkgs, requireNamespace, logical(1), quietly = TRUE)
        if (any(!ok)) { cat("FAILED to load:", paste(pkgs[!ok], collapse=", "), "\n"); quit(status=1) }
        stopifnot(utils::packageVersion("imcRtools") >= "1.6.0")
        cat("OK: imcRtools", as.character(utils::packageVersion("imcRtools")),
            "and", length(pkgs), "key packages load.\n")
    '

%help
    MapMetSC single-cell + spatial analysis image (Lazic et al.).

    A single image for the whole R workflow: analysis/, analysis_AD/ and
    analysis/07_spatial_analysis.Rmd. It bundles imcRtools 1.10.0
    (Bioconductor 3.19), which already contains the testInteractions fix that
    previously required a separate `lazdaria/mapmetsc_spatial` image.

    Data layout (see README): the scripts expect the extracted single-cell
    data under /mnt/data (input_all, input_AD, public_datasets, output).

    Render the full pipeline (headless):
      apptainer exec --bind /path/to/singlecelldata:/mnt/data \
          mapmetsc.sif Rscript run_analysis.R

    Render one script:
      apptainer exec --bind /path/to/singlecelldata:/mnt/data mapmetsc.sif \
          Rscript -e 'rmarkdown::render("analysis/07_spatial_analysis.Rmd",
                        output_dir="docs",
                        params=list(input="/mnt/data/input_all",
                                    output="/mnt/data/output"))'

    Interactive R:
      apptainer run --bind /path/to/singlecelldata:/mnt/data mapmetsc.sif

    RStudio Server (optional; the base image ships it). Apptainer containers
    are read-only, so redirect the server's writable dirs to a bind mount:
      mkdir -p rstudio-run/{tmp,var,run}
      PASSWORD=mapmetsc apptainer exec \
          --bind rstudio-run/var:/var/lib/rstudio-server \
          --bind rstudio-run/run:/var/run/rstudio-server \
          --bind rstudio-run/tmp:/tmp \
          --bind /path/to/MapMetSC:/home/rstudio/MapMetSC \
          --bind /path/to/singlecelldata:/mnt/data \
          mapmetsc.sif \
          /usr/lib/rstudio-server/bin/rserver --www-port 8787 \
              --auth-none 0 --auth-pam-helper-path=pam-helper --server-user=$(whoami)
      then open http://localhost:8787
